+	dsb();
+	can0_frame_state = CAN0_FRAME_EMPTY;
+
+	/* One bounded catch-up attempt only - not a drain loop. Mirrors
+	 * interrupt_main_handler()'s own "only touch SPI if idle" discipline;
+	 * if the bus isn't idle right now, this attempt is silently skipped
+	 * (not retried here) - the next call to this same function (next
+	 * loop iteration) will try again. can0_frame_dropped_count is
+	 * untouched by this path - it still means exactly what it meant
+	 * before (a frame the FIQ itself declined to capture because the
+	 * buffer was busy), not frames recovered here.
+	 *
+	 * TOCTOU fix: the EMPTY check, wait_for_spi_idle(), and
+	 * read_pending_rx_frame() below run with this core's own FIQ taking
+	 * masked, closing the race where the FIQ preempts between this
+	 * check and the read and independently captures+publishes a frame
+	 * that this call would otherwise clobber. This does NOT touch
+	 * GPIO25, FIQ_CONTROL, or interrupt routing - it only masks this
+	 * CPU's own local FIQ-taking (CPSR.F) for the few instructions of
+	 * this specific check-and-capture sequence, using the same
+	 * thread_get_exceptions()/thread_set_exceptions() pair
+	 * rpi3_can_server_loop() already uses in this project
+	 * (rpi3_can_server.c) - not a different or guessed API. THREAD_EXCP_NATIVE_INTR
+	 * is confirmed (out/arm/conf.mk: CFG_CORE_IRQ_IS_NATIVE_INTR=n) to
+	 * resolve to CPSR.F on this build, i.e. exactly the FIQ this file's
+	 * own CAN0 interrupt arrives as - the same bit
+	 * rpi3_can_server_loop() unmasks to receive it in the first place.
+	 *
+	 * The previous full exception state is saved before masking and
+	 * restored exactly afterward (thread_set_exceptions(exceptions), not
+	 * a blind unmask) - thread_set_exceptions() is a direct, absolute
+	 * set of the CPSR mask bits (core/arch/arm/kernel/thread.c), so
+	 * restoring the saved value returns every bit (including
+	 * THREAD_EXCP_FOREIGN_INTR) to precisely what it was, regardless of
+	 * what it happened to be before this function ran.
